thority - invoking Neurath, Dewey, Habermas without showing how their work actually supports ${subject}'s specific claims.`,\n  tuquoque: `'You too!' deflections that don't answer critiques - even when accurate, pointing to ${critic}'s problems doesn't solve ${subject}'s.`,\n  // Vulnerability streams - analyze the critic's counter-response for weaknesses\n  strawman_risk: `Passages where ${critic} characterizes ${subject} in ways ${subject} could credibly call misrepresentation - fix before he exploits it.`,\n  inconsistency: `Internal contradictions where ${critic} says one thing here and another there - gift-wrapped ammunition for ${subject}.`,\n  logic_gap: `Arguments where the conclusion doesn't follow from the premises - logical vulnerabilities ${subject} could drive a truck through.`,\n  unanswered: `Valid points ${subject} raised that ${critic} doesn't address - silences that look like evasion.`,\n  overconcession: `Places where ${critic} concedes too much - gifts to ${subject} that undermine ${critic}'s own position.`,\n  overreach: `Claims that extend beyond what the evidence supports - overstatements ${subject} can easily puncture.`,\n  undercitation: `Assertions about ${subject}'s framework without textual support - vulnerable to 'where do I say that?'`,\n  weak_authority: `Theorist invocations that don't actually support the claims - authority appeals ${subject} could challenge.`,\n  exposed_flank: `Critiques of ${subject} that could be turned back on ${critic} - tu quoque opportunities waiting to happen.`,\n  // Genealogy streams (only used in Arsenal, not in FindingsPage)\n  genealogy_ammunition: `Offensive findings sourced from intellectual genealogy analysis.`,\n  genealogy_revision: `Defensive revision items sourced from intellectual genealogy analysis.`\n});\n\n// Helper to extract last name from full name\nconst getLastName = fullName => fullName.split(' ').pop() || fullName;\n\n// Generate unique ID for findings\nconst generateFindingId = (strea