\\"appropriation\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Planning without prices becomes infrastructural coordination\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Benanav imports Neurath's non-price planning premise and turns it into an infrastructural coordination thesis.\\\", \\\"target_document_label\\\": \\\"Beyond Capitalism 2\\\", \\\"target_quote\\\": \\\"Coordination can be designed without handing the task back to prices.\\\", \\\"source_work_title\\\": \\\"Economic Plan and Calculation in Kind\\\", \\\"source_quote\\\": \\\"The economic plan can proceed in kind without price calculation.\\\", \\\"discrepancy_analysis\\\": \\\"The borrowing is strong, but Benanav updates the vocabulary to contemporary platform coordination.\\\", \\\"implication_for_argument\\\": \\\"This keeps planning legible after the critique of market socialism.\\\"}, {\\\"theme_id\\\": \\\"theme_calculation_without_prices\\\", \\\"theme_name\\\": \\\"Calculation Without Prices\\\", \\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"appropriation\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"War-economy coordination is rewritten as systems design\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"A wartime planning argument is reformulated as a general systems-design problem.\\\", \\\"target_document_label\\\": \\\"Beyond Capitalism 2\\\", \\\"target_quote\\\": \\\"Large-scale coordination is a design problem, not a market miracle.\\\", \\\"source_work_title\\\": \\\"Through War Economy to Economy in Kind\\\", \\\"source_quote\\\": \\\"War economy demonstrates directed allocation beyond market exchange.\\\", \\\"discrepancy_analysis\\\": \\\"Benanav abstracts away from the wartime setting while preserving the planning lesson.\\\", \\\"implication_for_argument\\\": \\\"It lets him universalize a historically bounded planning example.\\\"}, {\\\"theme_id\\\": \\\"theme_calculation_without_prices\\\", \\\"theme_name\\\": \\\"Calculation Without Prices\\\", \\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"misreading\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"In-kind accounting becomes computational administration\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The texture of Neurath's in-kind accounting is simplified into a computational administration claim.\\\", \\\"target_document_label\\\": \\\"Beyond Capitalism 2\\\", \\\"target_quote\\\": \\\"New infrastructures make administrative coordination tractable at scale.\\\", \\\"source_work_title\\\": \\\"Economic Plan and Calculation in Kind\\\", \\\"source_quote\\\": \\\"Calculation in kind depends on a rich material inventory, not merely faster computation.\\\", \\\"discrepancy_analysis\\\": \\\"Benanav compresses a substantive accounting doctrine into a tractability claim.\\\", \\\"implication_for_argument\\\": \\\"The simplification makes the contemporary case easier to state but thinner historically.\\\"}, {\\\"theme_id\\\": \\\"theme_calculation_without_prices\\\", \\\"theme_name\\\": \\\"Calculation Without Prices\\\", \\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"omission\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Statistical coordination eclipses material inventory work\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The planning argument underplays the administrative labor of maintaining material inventories.\\\", \\\"target_document_label\\\": \\\"Beyond Capitalism 2\\\", \\\"target_quote\\\": \\\"Coordination requires information systems that no longer need prices.\\\", \\\"source_work_title\\\": \\\"Socialist Utility Calculation and Capitalist Profit Calculation\\\", \\\"source_quote\\\": \\\"Statistical and material records are the basis of coordinated production.\\\", \\\"discrepancy_analysis\\\": \\\"Benanav keeps the conclusion while thinning the bureaucratic substrate.\\\", \\\"implication_for_argument\\\": \\\"This makes the argument cleaner but less institutionally grounded.\\\"}, {\\\"theme_id\\\": \\\"theme_planning_as_public_knowledge\\\", \\\"theme_name\\\": \\\"Planning as Public Knowledge\\\", \\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"compression\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Democratic intelligibility is present only as a side note\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Neurath's democratic pedagogy appears, but only as a subordinate implication.\\\", \\\"target_document_label\\\": \\\"Beyond Capitalism 2\\\", \\\"target_quote\\\": \\\"Coordination must still be socially intelligible.\\\", \\\"source_work_title\\\": \\\"International Planning for Freedom\\\", \\\"source_quote\\\": \\\"Planning must remain publicly discussable and democratically legible.\\\", \\\"discrepancy_analysis\\\": \\\"The civic dimension survives, but mostly as an appendix to the planning argument.\\\", \\\"implication_for_argument\\\": \\\"The result is a narrower, more technical reading of Neurath.\\\"}]}\",\"prose_ref_view_key\":null,\"items\":null,\"tab_count\":null,\"visibility\":\"if_data_exists\",\"position\":1.3,\"children\":[]},{\"view_key\":\"aoi_thematic_report\",\"view_name\":\"Report\",\"description\":\"Structured AOI closeout over the selected thinker: summary, engagement pattern, key divergences, sin distribution, and reading implications.\",\"renderer_type\":\"accordion\",\"renderer_config\":{\"sections\":[{\"key\":\"summary\",\"title\":\"Summary\"},{\"key\":\"engagement_pattern\",\"title\":\"Engagement Pattern\"},{\"key\":\"key_divergences\",\"title\":\"Key Divergences\"},{\"key\":\"sin_distribution\",\"title\":\"Sin Distribution\"},{\"key\":\"reading_implications\",\"title\":\"Reading Implications\"}],\"expand_first\":true,\"section_renderers\":{\"summary\":{\"renderer_type\":\"annotated_prose\",\"config\":{\"pull_quote_min_length\":90,\"section_description\":\"Bounded AOI closeout summary.\"}},\"engagement_pattern\":{\"renderer_type\":\"annotated_prose\",\"config\":{\"pull_quote_min_length\":90,\"section_description\":\"Overall pattern of Benanav's engagement with the selected source thinker.\"}},\"key_divergences\":{\"renderer_type\":\"mini_card_list\",\"config\":{\"title_field\":\"title\",\"subtitle_field\":\"subtitle\",\"description_field\":\"description\",\"badge_field\":\"badge\",\"section_description\":\"Highest-salience AOI divergences.\"}},\"sin_distribution\":{\"renderer_type\":\"mini_card_list\",\"config\":{\"title_field\":\"sin_type\",\"subtitle_field\":\"count\",\"description_field\":\"description\",\"section_description\":\"Distribution of findings across the AOI sin taxonomy.\"}},\"reading_implications\":{\"renderer_type\":\"annotated_prose\",\"config\":{\"pull_quote_min_length\":90,\"section_description\":\"What the bounded AOI result implies for reading Benanav's use of the selected source thinker.\"}}}},\"presentation_stance\":\"summary\",\"priority\":\"secondary\",\"rationale\":\"child of included parent\",\"data_quality\":\"standard\",\"top_level_group\":null,\"source_parent_view_key\":\"aoi_thematic_analysis\",\"promoted_to_top_level\":false,\"selection_priority\":\"secondary\",\"navigation_state\":\"normal\",\"structuring_policy\":null,\"semantic_scaffold_type\":\"none\",\"scaffold_hosting_mode\":\"none\",\"derivation_kind\":null,\"phase_number\":4.0,\"engine_key\":\"aoi_thematic_report\",\"chain_key\":null,\"scope\":\"aggregated\",\"has_structured_data\":true,\"structured_data\":{\"summary\":\"Benanav's AOI pattern is dominated by one planning theme, with a secondary civic-intelligibility strand that stays visible but subordinate.\",\"engagement_pattern\":\"The engagement is strongest when Benanav reframes Neurath's planning arguments as contemporary coordination problems and weaker when Neurath's democratic epistemology would need to be foregrounded.\",\"key_divergences\":[{\"title\":\"Planning becomes infrastructural coordination\",\"subtitle\":\"Calculation Without Prices\",\"description\":\"Benanav preserves the anti-price premise but redescribes it as infrastructural coordination.\",\"badge\":\"high\"},{\"title\":\"Democratic pedagogy is compressed\",\"subtitle\":\"Planning as Public Knowledge\",\"description\":\"Neurath's public-education emphasis appears only as a secondary implication.\",\"badge\":\"medium\"}],\"sin_distribution\":[{\"sin_type\":\"Appropriation\",\"count\":2,\"description\":\"Two findings show strong borrowing with updated language.\"},{\"sin_type\":\"Misreading\",\"count\":1,\"description\":\"One finding compresses Neurath's accounting doctrine into computational administration.\"}],\"reading_implications\":\"The dossier case reads Benanav as leaning heavily on one Neurathian planning strand while trimming the democratic and bureaucratic thickness that made the original view distinctive.\"},\"reading_scaffold\":null,\"raw_prose\":\"{\\\"report_sections\\\": {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Benanav's AOI pattern is dominated by one planning theme, with a secondary civic-intelligibility strand that stays visible but subordinate.\\\", \\\"engagement_pattern\\\": \\\"The engagement is strongest when Benanav reframes Neurath's planning arguments as contemporary coordination problems and weaker when Neurath's democratic epistemology would need to be foregrounded.\\\", \\\"key_divergences\\\": [{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Planning becomes infrastructural coordination\\\", \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Calculation Without Prices\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Benanav preserves the anti-price premise but redescribes it as infrastructural coordination.\\\", \\\"badge\\\": \\\"high\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Democratic pedagogy is compressed\\\", \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Planning as Public Knowledge\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Neurath's public-education emphasis appears only as a secondary implication.\\\", \\\"badge\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}], \\\"sin_distribution\\\": [{\\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"Appropriation\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Two findings show strong borrowing with updated language.\\\"}, {\\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"Misreading\\\", \\\"count\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"One finding compresses Neurath's accounting doctrine into computational administration.\\\"}], \\\"reading_implications\\\": \\\"The dossier case reads Benanav as leaning heavily on one 