dge\":\"medium\"}],\"sin_distribution\":[{\"sin_type\":\"Appropriation\",\"count\":2,\"description\":\"Two findings show strong borrowing with updated language.\"},{\"sin_type\":\"Misreading\",\"count\":1,\"description\":\"One finding compresses Neurath's accounting doctrine into computational administration.\"}],\"reading_implications\":\"The dossier case reads Benanav as leaning heavily on one Neurathian planning strand while trimming the democratic and bureaucratic thickness that made the original view distinctive.\"},\"reading_scaffold\":null,\"raw_prose\":\"{\\\"report_sections\\\": {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Benanav's AOI pattern is dominated by one planning theme, with a secondary civic-intelligibility strand that stays visible but subordinate.\\\", \\\"engagement_pattern\\\": \\\"The engagement is strongest when Benanav reframes Neurath's planning arguments as contemporary coordination problems and weaker when Neurath's democratic epistemology would need to be foregrounded.\\\", \\\"key_divergences\\\": [{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Planning becomes infrastructural coordination\\\", \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Calculation Without Prices\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Benanav preserves the anti-price premise but redescribes it as infrastructural coordination.\\\", \\\"badge\\\": \\\"high\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Democratic pedagogy is compressed\\\", \\\"subtitle\\\": \\\"Planning as Public Knowledge\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Neurath's public-education emphasis appears only as a secondary implication.\\\", \\\"badge\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}], \\\"sin_distribution\\\": [{\\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"Appropriation\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Two findings show strong borrowing with updated language.\\\"}, {\\\"sin_type\\\": \\\"Misreading\\\", \\\"count\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"One finding compresses Neurath's accounting doctrine into computational administration.\\\"}], \\\"reading_implications\\\": \\\"The dossier case reads Benanav as leaning heavily on one 